# Cloudflare Pages headers (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/)

# Allow the results submission tools to fetch the schedule feed cross-origin.
# This is a static public JSON file — the same information the schedule page
# already renders — and a plain GET is a CORS "simple request", so this single
# response header is the entire CORS surface.
#
# `*`, TO MATCH WHAT THE ZONE ALREADY SENDS. This rule was first written scoped
# to one origin, which was wrong in a way worth recording: something at the
# Cloudflare ZONE level sends `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` for every host on
# gpsaswimming.org — verified on paths with no `_headers` rule at all, and on
# css.gpsaswimming.org, which has no `_headers` file. A narrower value here is
# not enforced, so writing one states a restriction that is not in force and
# would break this feed's only consumer if the zone rule were ever removed.
#
# Everything served from this host is public, so `*` discloses nothing: it
# governs what browser JavaScript on another origin may read, not who may read.
/schedule.json
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

# The feed is rebuilt on every deploy and a stale copy would misidentify a
# rescheduled meet. Revalidate rather than serving from cache blind.
/schedule.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
